&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At HelloFresh, data is at the heart of everything we do — from the moment a customer places an order to the way we forecast demand, optimize our supply chain, and personalize experiences for millions of people. Making that data fast, reliable, and available is what our Data Platform makes possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Platform Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Operational Data Platform&lt;/strong&gt; team — the squad that ensures operational data is created, delivered, and shared downstream reliably, cost-efficiently, and with the quality guarantees that everything downstream depends on — so the analytics layer receives quality data, ready to be turned into governed assets. You will build the streaming, messaging, and self-service provisioning systems that hundreds of backend and data engineers rely on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on engineering role at the core of our platform. You&#39;ll own critical infrastructure, drive efficiency, and help define the &quot;golden path&quot; that makes it effortless for engineers across the company to store and stream their data — with governance and cost control built in from the start.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and run our streaming and messaging platform.&lt;/strong&gt; Own the systems that move data in real time and at scale — Kafka, Kafka Connect, Flink, and SQS — and keep them fast, resilient, and easy to build on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive efficiency.&lt;/strong&gt; Identify and act on opportunities to reduce the cost and complexity of the platform, and make efficiency a default rather than an afterthought.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the reliability of critical data paths.&lt;/strong&gt; Keep the systems at the

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;HelloFresh serves millions of customers weekly across 18 business units and 8 brands worldwide. At the heart of our product is a belief that every customer deserves a menu that feels like it was made for them, the right meals, at the right time, for the right person. We call it the Sous Chef vision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Senior PM II on the Personalization Experience team&lt;/strong&gt;, you own what makes that vision real and&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;felt&lt;/em&gt;. You&#39;re not building the ranking algorithm, you&#39;re building the experiences that make customers trust it, the data collection that makes it smart, and the moments where someone thinks: &lt;em&gt;this app actually knows me&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-autonomy role at the intersection of consumer UX, engineering, and ML systems. The problems are genuinely hard, the scale is real, and the decisions are yours to make.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Food Profile Quality &amp;amp; Signal Collection:&lt;/strong&gt; The food profile is the raw material that powers everything downstream. Your job is to move customers from &quot;fields filled in&quot; to truly Personalization-Ready: high-signal, validated, actionable. You&#39;ll own and iterate on the collection experiences that give our models the data they need to perform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The &quot;Sous Chef&quot; Feel &amp;amp; Transparency:&lt;/strong&gt; You build the moments where personalization becomes tangible, the places where we tell customers &lt;em&gt;why&lt;/em&gt; certain meals were chosen for them. This isn&#39;t just UX work, it&#39;s trust infrastructure for the entire personalization stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Org Data Supplier&l

&lt;p&gt;You know database development inside out, and you love talking about the tools that make it better. You spend your time where data professionals gather, sharing insights and helping others solve real problems. If you want to step away from daily query writing and start shaping the community around a product you believe in, this role is for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JetBrains&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We create intelligent software development tools for developers and teams. More than 15 million users, over 300,000 organizations, and 88 of the Fortune Global Top 100 companies rely on our products to solve real, complex problems. Our mission is simple: make development teams more productive and AI adoptable at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DataGrip is a core part of our ecosystem and revenue, but we currently lack a dedicated face to represent it to the outside world. We are looking for a Developer Advocate to take ownership of our public presence within developer communities and connect with our global users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will bridge the gap between our users and our product team. You will bring DataGrip to the center of the conversation by diving into online discussions, crafting advocacy content that provides value for years to come, and gathering the real-world feedback we need to build better tools. When we build and launch new database products, you will be involved in the product discussions from inception, leading the way.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Day to day, you will&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and join active conversations across platforms like X, Reddit, and Discord to support database professionals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high-quality, long-lasting content, including videos and blog posts, that helps users master our tools.&lt

&lt;p&gt;At JetBrains, code is our passion. Ever since we started back in 2000, we have strived to create the strongest and most effective developer tools in the world. Today, we are evolving beyond standalone tools toward a unified, AI-native platform for software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is no longer just an assistant inside the editor – it is becoming an active participant in how software is planned, built, reviewed, and operated across teams and organizations. This shift brings challenges that cannot be solved at the level of individual tools alone, challenges that involve governance, security, cost control, observability, and coordination between humans and autonomous agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The &lt;strong&gt;JetBrains Platform team (JCP)&lt;/strong&gt; is building the foundation that connects developer workflows, team-level collaboration, and organizational control into a single coherent system. The platform is both deeply integrated with JetBrains products and designed to work across teams, products, and environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re now looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join an identity management and access team in JCP. The team owns several services responsible for authentication and authorization, as well as for managing organizations, user memberships, groups, and workspaces. All these form a foundational dependency for the rest of the platform. We also supply and support robust authentication components used by YouTrack, IDE Services, License Vault, Qodana, and other JetBrains products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the entire SDLC: codebase, architecture, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and evolve the services in Kotlin and a little bit of Go, ensuring reliability and performance as the platform grow

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team description&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp&#39;s Hardware Development team builds the physical products millions of small businesses rely on every day, and this role sits right at the start of a new chapter: moving our in-house hardware onto the Android platform for the first time. This isn&#39;t a typical Android device, it&#39;s a highly customised, security-first product built from scratch, which means the person joining will help define how the operating system, drivers, and secure processor come together rather than inheriting someone else&#39;s setup. The team works closely with hardware, software, and QA engineers across the bring-up process, so this role offers a rare chance to shape a product&#39;s foundations while working alongside experienced embedded and secure processor leads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system bring-up for the new Android embedded platform, from bootloader through to kernel and framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate and maintain kernel modules and drivers, including power management and connectivity components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to build system integration across the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug hardware and software issues at the protocol level and help resolve critical issues found during testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Carry out testing and validation to confirm the platform is stable and secure before release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing embedded systems with a strong focus on Android OS, gained over several years in a professional setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of the Android OS architecture, from bootloader (U-Boot, Little Kernel) and kernel through to frame

